WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:18.808
The faint, reddish light from Zing's breath showed Zann that he and his friends were in a stone passageway.

2
00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:22.825
The place had a damp, dusty smell that tickled Zann's nose.

3
00:00:22.826 --> 00:00:26.018
"Careful," Perda whispered as they started walking.

4
00:00:26.019 --> 00:00:29.051
"We don't know what could be hiding down here."

5
00:00:29.052 --> 00:00:31.643
Zann tried not to think about that.

6
00:00:31.644 --> 00:00:37.950
He kept his gaze on Zing, who flew ahead, letting out an occasional burst of flame to light the way.

7
00:00:37.951 --> 00:00:43.344
Suddenly Zing spun around and leaped at him. "Whoa!" Zann cried.

8
00:00:43.345 --> 00:00:47.875
"What's the matter with you? This is no time for our game!"

9
00:00:47.876 --> 00:00:50.412
He tried to push the dragon aside.

10
00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:54.744
But Zing spat fire at him, narrowly missing Zann's arm.

11
00:00:54.745 --> 00:00:58.415
"Zing!" Zann scolded again. "Stop—"

12
00:00:58.416 --> 00:01:03.003
"Wait," Darb told Zann. "He might be trying to tell us something."

13
00:01:03.004 --> 00:01:08.157
Perda peered past them. "Look," she said. "There's a hole!"

14
00:01:08.158 --> 00:01:15.676
Zing relaxed and backed off. He scampered to the edge of the drop-off, blowing out a sheet of flame so they could see better.

15
00:01:15.677 --> 00:01:20.615
Zann gulped as he looked down. The hole was at least ten feet deep.

16
00:01:20.616 --> 00:01:23.573
And something at the bottom was moving.

17
00:01:23.574 --> 00:01:27.307
"What's down there?" Gliss sounded horrified.

18
00:01:27.308 --> 00:01:31.351
"It looks like a nest of cave hissers." Darb shuddered.

19
00:01:31.352 --> 00:01:35.779
"This must be a trap in case anyone tried to follow the king or queen."

20
00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:38.949
He patted Zing. "Thanks for the warning, little buddy."

21
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.659
They picked their way carefully around the pit.

22
00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.684
After that nobody talked much. They just walked.

23
00:01:45.685 --> 00:01:50.314
And walked. And then walked some more.

24
00:01:50.315 --> 00:01:56.043
The tunnel took so many twists and turns that Zann completely lost his bearings.

25
00:01:56.044 --> 00:02:01.402
Then Zing stopped again. "Look! There's a fork in the tunnel," Darb said.

26
00:02:01.403 --> 00:02:06.527
"Which way should we go?" asked Perda. "Both tunnels go up."

27
00:02:06.528 --> 00:02:11.301
"Well, we have to take one of them," said Gliss. "I vote we go that way."

28
00:02:11.302 --> 00:02:13.966
Gliss pointed at the left-hand tunnel.

29
00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:17.918
They followed Zing's glowing breath up the tunnel.

30
00:02:17.919 --> 00:02:21.071
"Careful," Zann said as he stumbled over something.

31
00:02:21.072 --> 00:02:23.461
"There's a rock on the floor here."

32
00:02:23.462 --> 00:02:26.424
He waved the others past him so they wouldn't trip.

33
00:02:26.425 --> 00:02:30.123
Then he glanced down at the object on the floor.

34
00:02:30.124 --> 00:02:37.893
His eyes widened. "I was wrong, you guys," he said. "It's not a rock. It's a bone!"

35
00:02:37.894 --> 00:02:42.175
"What?" Gliss squeaked. "What kind of bone?"

36
00:02:42.176 --> 00:02:47.088
Suddenly a terrible howl echoed through the tunnel behind them.

37
00:02:47.089 --> 00:02:51.080
A huge, dark beast emerged right out of the wall!

38
00:02:51.081 --> 00:02:54.792
"Oh no! It's a shadow beast!" Darb shouted.

39
00:02:54.793 --> 00:02:57.275
"A what?" Perda exclaimed.

40
00:02:57.276 --> 00:03:00.805
"I didn't think they really existed." Darb sounded scared.

41
00:03:00.806 --> 00:03:03.583
"Run!" Zann yelled.

42
00:03:03.584 --> 00:03:07.193
They ran up the tunnel with the shadow beast chasing them.

43
00:03:07.194 --> 00:03:11.523
Perda was in the lead, but after a short distance, she skidded to a stop.

44
00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:14.607
"Dead end!" she cried breathlessly.

45
00:03:14.608 --> 00:03:19.367
Zann looked back, terrified. The monster was lurching right toward them!

46
00:03:19.368 --> 00:03:25.478
Just then Zing flew toward the beast, sending out a burst of flame and lighting up the whole tunnel.

47
00:03:25.479 --> 00:03:29.889
To everyone's amazement the shadow beast disappeared for a moment!

48
00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:36.454
"That's right!" Darb said. "Shadow beasts have to stay in the dark. The light destroys them."

49
00:03:36.455 --> 00:03:41.188
Zing continued to breathe fire while everyone quickly ran back down the tunnel.

50
00:03:41.189 --> 00:03:46.785
They reached the fork and dashed up the right-hand tunnel. Zing soon followed.

51
00:03:46.786 --> 00:03:50.189
"Whew, that was close," Perda said.

52
00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:54.567
"Yeah," Gliss said. "I hope this tunnel leads to the palace.

53
00:03:54.568 --> 00:03:58.058
Because I definitely don't want to pass that thing again!"

54
00:03:58.059 --> 00:04:02.104
Nobody answered. They all just started walking again.

55
00:04:02.105 --> 00:04:06.813
And soon they were climbing as the tunnel grew steeper and steeper.

56
00:04:06.814 --> 00:04:11.189
Just when Zann was starting to think they'd be climbing forever, Darb spoke.

57
00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:14.897
"Is it my imagination, or is it getting lighter in here?"

58
00:04:14.898 --> 00:04:20.324
Zann suddenly realized Darb was right. "There must be an opening nearby!"

59
00:04:20.325 --> 00:04:27.253
They hurried around the next corner. Just up ahead, pale light poured in through an opening at the end of the tunnel!

60
00:04:27.254 --> 00:04:35.334
The opening was large enough for a person to squeeze through—except it was completely crisscrossed with stout iron bars.

61
00:04:35.335 --> 00:04:39.263
"I think we found the palace!" Gliss exclaimed.

62
00:04:39.264 --> 00:04:42.592
Zann pressed his face against the iron bars.

63
00:04:42.593 --> 00:04:46.019
The opening was located near the floor of a large room.

64
00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:50.679
A pair of golden chairs stood in the center of the polished floor.

65
00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:54.282
"This must be the throne room!" Zann whispered.

66
00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:57.478
"Then where is everybody?" Perda murmured.

67
00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:06.291
Zann shrugged. "I'm sure the king and queen don't spend all their time here," he said. "All we have to do is wait for—"

68
00:05:06.292 --> 00:05:10.361
The crash of doors flying open drowned out the rest of his words.

69
00:05:10.362 --> 00:05:14.751
About a dozen people rushed into the throne room, talking loudly.

70
00:05:14.752 --> 00:05:19.087
Zann couldn't follow most of what they were saying, but they sounded upset.

71
00:05:19.088 --> 00:05:25.548
"Isn't that the queen?" Perda pointed to a statuesque woman with bright red hair.

72
00:05:25.549 --> 00:05:30.583
Zann nodded. "I see the king too. Let's try to get their attention."

73
00:05:30.584 --> 00:05:34.107
Before he could yell, there was a blinding flash of light.

74
00:05:34.108 --> 00:05:37.192
Zann had to squeeze his eyes shut for a second.

75
00:05:37.193 --> 00:05:40.404
When he opened them, the scene had changed.

76
00:05:40.405 --> 00:05:47.618
Morb was in the throne room, along with a dozen trolls and at least fifty tiny, stinging dragons!

77
00:05:47.619 --> 00:05:51.555
"No!" someone screamed. "Your Majesties—"

78
00:05:51.556 --> 00:05:55.122
"Get back!" the king's deep voice roared.

79
00:05:55.123 --> 00:06:00.053
Others were also shouting, screaming, or calling out various spells.

80
00:06:00.054 --> 00:06:04.263
Above the din Zann could hear Morb's chilling laugh.

81
00:06:04.264 --> 00:06:09.184
There was another flash of light. Thick, choking smoke filled the room.

82
00:06:09.185 --> 00:06:12.536
When it cleared, the scene had changed again.

83
00:06:12.537 --> 00:06:17.752
The king and queen were gone, along with the few other Reds who had been present.

84
00:06:17.753 --> 00:06:23.389
The trolls and dragons were gone too. Everyone else was frozen or unconscious.

85
00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:33.879
Morb had also vanished. But Zann could still hear the fading echo of his terrible cackle.
